    "intro": {
      "title": "GameCraft",
      "subtitle": "The 4th Game Development Event at Amirkabir University of Technology",
      "description": "GameCraft is a game development event aimed at inspiring and nurturing passion in game design enthusiasts. Hosted by Amirkabir University of Technology, this year's event focuses on creating a platform for knowledge transfer and networking among game development experts.\nThe event includes in-person workshops, presentations, and a game development competition. Winners will be recognized and awarded at the closing ceremony."
    },
    "aboutUs": {
      "title": "About Us",
      "description": "The Computer Science Student Association at Amirkabir University is an independent organization dedicated to scientific and educational activities. Each year, the association hosts numerous academic and educational events at university, national, and international levels, attracting a large audience. Notable events include ACM competitions, Linux festivals, DMC data mining competitions, and AAISS artificial intelligence seminars.\nOne of the association's key approaches is strengthening team spirit and large-scale collaboration, helping students gain valuable experience for their professional lives. This event is no exception, with many students actively participating in the association's initiatives."
    },
